Instruction:
drm/i915: Fix a bug where the memory allocation for the jump whitelist was wrong.

The jump whitelist was allocated from the start of the batch, instead of the
end of it. This caused the jump whitelist to be invalid when used to validate
commands that were found to be illegal.

Fixes: 7d9c9f8b8a1e ("drm/i915: Add support for Intel's new command parsing")
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
Reviewed-by: Christian Hergert <christian.hergert@intel.com>
Link: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20230111110000.11011-1-davem@davemloft.net
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

